Here's an example of how you could define the service layer for your sensor data and wildlife sightings:

**SensorDataService.java**
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class SensorDataService {
    private final SensorDataRepository sensorDataRepository;

    @Autowired
    public SensorDataService(SensorDataRepository sensorDataRepository) {
        this.sensorDataRepository = sensorDataRepository;
    }

    public List<SensorData> getAllSensorData() {
        return sensorDataRepository.findAll();
    }

    public SensorData getSensorDataById(Long id) {
        return sensorDataRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    }

    public SensorData createSensorData(SensorData sensorData) {
        return sensorDataRepository.save(sensorData);
    }

    public SensorData updateSensorData(Long id, SensorData updatedSensorData) {
        SensorData existingSensorData = getSensorDataById(id);
        existingSensorData.setTemperature(updatedSensorData.getTemperature());
        existingSensorData.setSalinity(updatedSensorData.getSalinity());
        existingSensorData.setAcousticPing(updatedSensorData.getAcousticPing());
        return sensorDataRepository.save(existingSensorData);
    }

    public void deleteSensorData(Long id) {
        sensorDataRepository.deleteById(id);
    }
}
```
**WildlifeSightingService.java**
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class WildlifeSightingService {
    private final WildlifeSightingRepository wildlifeSightingRepository;

    @Autowired
    public WildlifeSightingService(WildlifeSightingRepository wildlifeSightingRepository) {
        this.wildlifeSightingRepository = wildlifeSightingRepository;
    }

    public List<WildlifeSighting> getAllWildlifeSightings() {
        return wildlifeSightingRepository.findAll();
    }

    public WildlifeSighting getWildlifeSightingById(Long id) {
        return wildlifeSightingRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    }

    public WildlifeSighting createWildlifeSighting(WildlifeSighting wildlifeSighting) {
        return wildlifeSightingRepository.save(wildlifeSighting);
    }

    public WildlifeSighting updateWildlifeSighting(Long id, WildlifeSighting updatedWildlifeSighting) {
        WildlifeSighting existingWildlifeSighting = getWildlifeSightingById(id);
        existingWildlifeSighting.setSpecies(updatedWildlifeSighting.getSpecies());
        existingWildlifeSighting.setLocation(updatedWildlifeSighting.getLocation());
        existingWildlifeSighting.setTimestamp(updatedWildlifeSighting.getTimestamp());
        return wildlifeSightingRepository.save(existingWildlifeSighting);
    }

    public void deleteWildlifeSighting(Long id) {
        wildlifeSightingRepository.deleteById(id);
    }
}
```
These services provide a layer of abstraction between the controller and repository layers, encapsulating the business logic
of your application.

